[{:db/id "q-79932/selection/3b762d884f5fe0fa2265ff1e469e0bb5bcf19c59a850310d5f5054c22e921ac1" :answer/id #uuid "ad907199-f13a-5f57-b5e6-e24f4579d028" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x/2}+B{e}^{-x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79932/selection/f04b68112cc72acadddf6e5c1da827c9736a870b7cc6dd6522aa8e720769464e" :answer/id #uuid "c34b8e6f-3b2d-5272-a328-1794ea50aaab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{-x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79932/selection/eba2f67583e744db1e927eea73a03d75d8cb9f1286779edf4f826802a4a294ca" :answer/id #uuid "4c72ef9b-4587-5060-bed7-8b3b781c9a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79932/selection/ec31f789fb0dbfa029c446c6a137eaccfd024bc6ef28d8b4857b47431b105b90" :answer/id #uuid "f33e58a8-d0f4-54fa-9af7-2068f0cbcbf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x/2}+B{e}^{x/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79932/selection/0b0fbb864e866854d13c9fed152dc4f1003f9abe76e8358bab7feb68d4103ec6" :answer/id #uuid "c8d93e63-ee9f-5c7d-bd77-ae65ac577d3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{x/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79932/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "89eec56d-e3c9-5f1f-9751-f0df759ff987" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79932/selection/eba2f67583e744db1e927eea73a03d75d8cb9f1286779edf4f826802a4a294ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-79932/selection/3b762d884f5fe0fa2265ff1e469e0bb5bcf19c59a850310d5f5054c22e921ac1" "q-79932/selection/f04b68112cc72acadddf6e5c1da827c9736a870b7cc6dd6522aa8e720769464e" "q-79932/selection/eba2f67583e744db1e927eea73a03d75d8cb9f1286779edf4f826802a4a294ca" "q-79932/selection/ec31f789fb0dbfa029c446c6a137eaccfd024bc6ef28d8b4857b47431b105b90" "q-79932/selection/0b0fbb864e866854d13c9fed152dc4f1003f9abe76e8358bab7feb68d4103ec6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79932" :question/id #uuid "25f76d61-f5bd-5300-a8bb-fba17cb3162f" :question/math-academy-id "q-79932" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x/2}$ is a solution to the equation $4{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+y=0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x){e}^{x/2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{x/2}+\\frac{u}{2}{e}^{x/2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{x/2}+{u}^{′}{e}^{x/2}+\\frac{u}{4}{e}^{x/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({u}^{″}{e}^{x/2}+{u}^{′}{e}^{x/2}+\\frac{u}{4}{e}^{x/2})-4({u}^{′}{e}^{x/2}+\\frac{u}{2}{e}^{x/2})+u{e}^{x/2} & =0 \\\\ 4{u}^{″}{e}^{x/2}+4{u}^{′}{e}^{x/2}+u{e}^{x/2}-4{u}^{′}{e}^{x/2}-2u{e}^{x/2}+u{e}^{x/2} & =0 \\\\ 4{u}^{″}{e}^{x/2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $4{e}^{x/2}\\ne 0$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the equation twice gives\n\n$$\nu={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThus, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{e}^{x/2}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x/2}({c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x/2}\\cdot x=x{e}^{x/2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})={e}^{x}\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{x/2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79932/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67ca0bc-c946-5963-a733-2ec9eb6b07ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79932"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79935/selection/282c24906206ea8d23f85b08f5e11d68fc857fc42886f8a292dedcfbde904ecf" :answer/id #uuid "3e1f53c9-5627-58c5-b1cd-8d0e7465676e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{2}+B{x}^{-3/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79935/selection/015e991beed5513719702caf71580de747e3775fb729e0f3c08f39d07b66a1bc" :answer/id #uuid "579e8f34-c144-5f56-99b3-f9d9d7e2a4e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{2}+B{x}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79935/selection/f44c7de01513535c49235ac7c3d74895908396d1c459aa619fe92d3efa46607f" :answer/id #uuid "e24316b7-d6b2-5c8c-9234-8f29428f44ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{2}+B{x}^{3/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79935/selection/b2521b8292b83240d0ad831bfa133aea8291fd4b9caee7d30648e109a01cd61c" :answer/id #uuid "a048e4a0-9260-5af6-8718-630f35b6372a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{2}+B{x}^{1/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79935/selection/a9bfa986f590b2d372b64601350161f9f4ada7581e17b23551dab0461bf327a9" :answer/id #uuid "666defca-4628-53b7-ab19-517f60e736f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{2}+B{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79935/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "268af40b-d4fd-56b6-b810-7de22bde78dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79935/selection/b2521b8292b83240d0ad831bfa133aea8291fd4b9caee7d30648e109a01cd61c" :answer-field/choices ["q-79935/selection/282c24906206ea8d23f85b08f5e11d68fc857fc42886f8a292dedcfbde904ecf" "q-79935/selection/015e991beed5513719702caf71580de747e3775fb729e0f3c08f39d07b66a1bc" "q-79935/selection/f44c7de01513535c49235ac7c3d74895908396d1c459aa619fe92d3efa46607f" "q-79935/selection/b2521b8292b83240d0ad831bfa133aea8291fd4b9caee7d30648e109a01cd61c" "q-79935/selection/a9bfa986f590b2d372b64601350161f9f4ada7581e17b23551dab0461bf327a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79935" :question/id #uuid "3624b381-ff5b-5c61-a5d8-e12407af8abd" :question/math-academy-id "q-79935" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation $2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-3x{y}^{′}+2y=0$ for $x>0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x){x}^{2}.$\n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{x}^{2}+2ux \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{x}^{2}+4{u}^{′}x+2u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}({u}^{″}{x}^{2}+4{u}^{′}x+2u)-3x({u}^{′}{x}^{2}+2ux)+2(u{x}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2{u}^{″}{x}^{4}+8{u}^{′}{x}^{3}+4u{x}^{2}-3{u}^{′}{x}^{3}-6u{x}^{2}+2u{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{u}^{″}{x}^{4}+5{u}^{′}{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}(2x{u}^{″}+5{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${x}^{3}\\ne 0$ for $x>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n2x{u}^{″}+5{u}^{′}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n2x{w}^{′}+5w=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}{x}^{-5/2}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}{x}^{-5/2}\\,⟹\\,u=-\\frac{2{c}_{1}}{3}{x}^{-3/2}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{x}^{2}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=(-\\frac{2{c}_{1}}{3}{x}^{-3/2}+{c}_{2}){x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=({x}^{-3/2}){x}^{2}={x}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2}\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{x}^{2}+B{x}^{1/2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79935/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef8a6ef-3e77-5e3e-ac75-c3dece0af96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79935"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90763/selection/d07e6ec3e7c05002cd8b866b50107157a7a35a8f0236b165b0ed92bf65643cb3" :answer/id #uuid "8e5e5b0e-8ff9-57fd-9029-4ca94e849004" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{3}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90763/selection/b7dacd46dbcad5164e7a5cf4d8d25a520515602d4905d9c77062ac4184f86e84" :answer/id #uuid "9f2da10b-0985-558d-826d-eac0a9c976c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{3}+Bx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90763/selection/4b8cae54f5ff361f2bf1f66c3b3d11ab9878883675b94191141b242929e38883" :answer/id #uuid "8ec54203-c9ef-58d3-9bfe-87f2f076f65e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{3}+B{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90763/selection/41f8bdfec5359cc49f550d22077e93e06940a4bbfdc6709a34c56e563d7ee13a" :answer/id #uuid "028a880e-33f9-5152-9520-1f3ddd7e6c29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{3}+B{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90763/selection/fc90d5af8e948de2bfd8da64ac4d5673653f31cba282bbd8dea33189ff3e4168" :answer/id #uuid "a37c98b0-7487-5ee9-92a5-4144dd85344c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{3}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90763/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b787034-cdbd-54cb-884d-5854355abc58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90763/selection/d07e6ec3e7c05002cd8b866b50107157a7a35a8f0236b165b0ed92bf65643cb3" :answer-field/choices ["q-90763/selection/d07e6ec3e7c05002cd8b866b50107157a7a35a8f0236b165b0ed92bf65643cb3" "q-90763/selection/b7dacd46dbcad5164e7a5cf4d8d25a520515602d4905d9c77062ac4184f86e84" "q-90763/selection/4b8cae54f5ff361f2bf1f66c3b3d11ab9878883675b94191141b242929e38883" "q-90763/selection/41f8bdfec5359cc49f550d22077e93e06940a4bbfdc6709a34c56e563d7ee13a" "q-90763/selection/fc90d5af8e948de2bfd8da64ac4d5673653f31cba282bbd8dea33189ff3e4168"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90763" :question/id #uuid "c467ed53-f0ee-5801-b4aa-ed3fa391372c" :question/math-academy-id "q-90763" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-6y=0$ for $x>0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x){x}^{3}.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{x}^{3}+3u{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{x}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{x}^{2}+6ux.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}({u}^{″}{x}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{x}^{2}+6ux)-6(u{x}^{3}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}({u}^{″}{x}^{2}+6{u}^{′}x+6u-6u) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}({u}^{″}{x}^{2}+6{u}^{′}x) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{4}({u}^{″}x+6{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${x}^{4}\\ne 0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}x+6{u}^{′}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\nx{w}^{′}+6w=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{{x}^{6}}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{{x}^{6}}\\,⟹\\,u=-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{5{x}^{5}}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{x}^{3}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={x}^{3}(-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{5{x}^{5}}+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=-5$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=-5\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{x}^{3}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-90763/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef8a6ef-3e77-5e3e-ac75-c3dece0af96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90763"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129957/selection/718ef10fa06ae21d2b758413eceb43061b6682337625d64a6e5062f7a53bd1b3" :answer/id #uuid "e39dbe18-f115-5185-bfda-4452826d62e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{4t}+B{t}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129957/selection/47da64355feddf5922c0a57981a379f84581d62fe628505e34b73d528bee97cd" :answer/id #uuid "84655674-afa3-5a63-8c65-2e82b4512494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{4t}+B{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129957/selection/84ba16fe0600ec9aca61bacbab55326604ce059277be359ffef13d30b9a2e281" :answer/id #uuid "c575c40a-3b6b-590b-8f58-bd27f16719c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{4t}+B{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129957/selection/0d7d02daa94ff0b1abf5b9a569cbb499effc4e88dd66f0ab168d4da20321c0a4" :answer/id #uuid "aae460c7-0e1f-569b-bec4-226c4f1ef6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{4t}+Bt{e}^{4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129957/selection/8987af0174083517cbf289eb7390059dfdd703c9be17aec8e64bc4566b4bf376" :answer/id #uuid "fdc8d2dc-caa5-54f8-86f7-dba73b353657" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{4t}+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129957/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3f33fb8-e98b-5cf5-92e4-d3998c8c60fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129957/selection/84ba16fe0600ec9aca61bacbab55326604ce059277be359ffef13d30b9a2e281" :answer-field/choices ["q-129957/selection/718ef10fa06ae21d2b758413eceb43061b6682337625d64a6e5062f7a53bd1b3" "q-129957/selection/47da64355feddf5922c0a57981a379f84581d62fe628505e34b73d528bee97cd" "q-129957/selection/84ba16fe0600ec9aca61bacbab55326604ce059277be359ffef13d30b9a2e281" "q-129957/selection/0d7d02daa94ff0b1abf5b9a569cbb499effc4e88dd66f0ab168d4da20321c0a4" "q-129957/selection/8987af0174083517cbf289eb7390059dfdd703c9be17aec8e64bc4566b4bf376"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129957" :question/id #uuid "f2fac4e5-7135-5e39-8138-1f3b4b97226e" :question/math-academy-id "q-129957" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(t)={e}^{4t}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}-16y=0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(t)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(t){e}^{4t}.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{4t}+4u{e}^{4t} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{4t}+8{u}^{′}{e}^{4t}+16u{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({u}^{″}{e}^{4t}+8{u}^{′}{e}^{4t}+16u{e}^{4t})-16u{e}^{4t} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{e}^{4t}+8{u}^{′}{e}^{4t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{4t}({u}^{″}+8{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{4t}\\ne 0$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}+8{u}^{′}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}+8w=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}{e}^{-8t}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}{e}^{-8t}\\,⟹\\,u=-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{8}{e}^{-8t}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(t)=u{e}^{4t}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=(-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{8}{e}^{-8t}+{c}_{2}){e}^{4t}.\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=-8$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-8t}\\cdot {e}^{4t}={e}^{-4t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=-8\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4t}+B{e}^{-4t}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129957/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67ca0bc-c946-5963-a733-2ec9eb6b07ce"] :knowl